Z||000000||Ken Wittlief||05-07-2001||10:34 AM||||I have been topping my tank off frequently, trying to get a good handle on my mpg (up to 15 at last fillup).<P>Its kinda creepy cause the pump shuts off, and then I can squeeze two more gallons into the tank before the gas comes up to the filler neck! I was acutally looking under the car to see if it was leaking out somewhere.<P>  Anyway - last time I topped off the tank I noticed the inside of the car smelled like gas, even with the windows open. The smell was still there till I put about 30 miles on it (about a day later).<BR>   Does this sound like the top of my fuel tank is leaking, oozing, gas? Does the filler pipe run anywhere that could cause a gas smell inside the car if a connection is loose? Could I have gotten gas into the evaporation canister when I filled it right to the cap?<P>   I kept checking and dont see any leaks or wet gas spots anywhere on the underside of the car.||||reg||1
Z||000001||84Bill||05-07-2001||11:21 AM||||Probably pupmed fuel into your vapor canister(not a really good thing) you should consider not topping it off that much then look into replacing the filter on the bottom of the canister itself. See the Ogres cave on this issue (Emissions) under the engin dropdown.<p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 05-07-2001).]||||reg||11
Z||000002||rogergarrison||05-07-2001||04:31 PM||||youll notice too, if you just pop up the sunroof in back, at highway speed the airflow will suck fumes into the passenger compartment, in town is ok. No fumes if you either leave it shut on freeway, or take it completely out. Popped up at speed the glass acts like a NACA duct, creating a vacum at the back that draws the air from the top engine vents inside.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jay||05-07-2001||06:15 PM||||To find the leak just light a match!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Sorry I couldn't resist!!  Ditto to everything mentioned above.||||reg||1
